      "observation": "Local recorded sales price trend is 'rising', with 102 closed transactions in the trailing 12 months and a median comp price of $1,154/sqft. This micro signal confirms seller momentum is still active in the immediate submarket, partially offsetting the macro deceleration concern.",
      "sources": ["NYC Open Data — DOF Rolling Calendar Sales (usep-8jbt)"]
    },
    {
      "observation": "Comp $/sqft readings are dispersed but several recent closings print above the $1,154 median — 173 8TH STREET closed at $1,507/sqft in October 2025 and 171 8 STREET at $1,128/sqft in May 2026 — indicating the market is still repricing upward on quality assets, though the wide spread (from $575 to $1,507/sqft) signals significant price sensitivity to property condition and timing.",
      "sources": ["NYC Open Data — DOF Rolling Calendar Sales (usep-8jbt)"]
    },
    {
      "observation": "The 30-year fixed mortgage rate at 6.65% is a meaningful affordability headwind. Against a tract median home value of $1,629,900, financing costs are substantial and compress the buyer pool, limiting upside velocity and increasing transaction risk for leveraged buyers.",
      "sources": ["Freddie Mac Primary Mortgage Market Survey (PMMS)", "US Census ACS via Census Reporter (ACS 2024 5-year)"]
    },
    {
      "observation": "HUD FMR for a 2-bedroom is $2,910/month (FY2026). Against a $1.6M+ acquisition price, gross rent yield on a two-family asset in this tract is thin — roughly 2.1% on a 2BR basis — suggesting investor yield support is weak and price sustainability depends more on appreciation expectations than income.",
      "sources": ["HUD USER — Fair Market Rents", "US Census ACS via Census Reporter (ACS 2024 5-year)"]
    }
  ],
  "minority_signals": [
    {
      "signal": "Recorded sales price trend is 'rising' with 102 transactions in 12 months, indicating active local demand and seller momentum.",
      "note": "Local momentum is real but insufficient to overcome the combination of a 45% five-year HPI run, 6.65% rates, and thin rental yield — these macro and structural factors dominate the timing read and argue against urgency to buy."
    }
  ]
}

